{
  "case_id": "2001-00-730",
  "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WILLIAM P. PENDLEY, ESQ., President and Chief Legal Advisor, Denver, Colorado; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nTHEODORE B. OLSON, ESQ., Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand Constructors, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1989, the small family business that is Adarand lost a Federal contract because of a racial program and the race of its owner, Randy Pesh."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand Constructors, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, Your Honor. The evidence is quite clear that the program still exists in Colorado."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Pendley, treat, if you will, fairly shortly coming up in your argument, the Government says that in a direct procurement program, these sort of preferences that you're challenging are simply not used in Colorado. You say they are. Do we simply have a factual dispute here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand Constructors, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The subcontracting compensation clause is still alive and it still applies against Adarand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand Constructors, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, on the issue of standing or mootness, this Court held in 1995 that Adarand had standing, and as the Court said in its Adarand 2000 opinion, in the Adarand case and in the Laidlaw case, the issue is now is not an issue of standing but one of mootness."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand Constructors, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PENDLEY: That's -- that's what our lodging demonstrates, Mr. Chief Justice. It demonstrates the United States is today still using in Colorado the mandatory subcontracting clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But to the extent that your -- your answer, in effect, tells us that the controversy is live and presented based on what you have in a lodging, you're really asking us to make a -- a determination of fact in a disagreement between you and the Government as to whether they're being used or whether they're not being used. And doesn't it make much more sense for us to send -- if that's what the case is going to turn on, doesn't it make much more sense for us to send it back to facts -- to courts that engage in fact-finding and that will make that determination on the basis of evidence as distinguished from our making it on the basis of a lodging?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm asserting that it violates law and it violates the regulation. It violates 48 C.F.R. 19201."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adarand",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so -- so, Adarand files this lodging and says, wait, look, they're still using these FAR's and they're hurting us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: This Court is a court of review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States is still -- it still has mechanisms. It's still using it against Adarand notwithstanding its attempt to tell this Court --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are no findings, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But are the benchmark studies conducted every year?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Olson",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Department of Commerce thereafter conducted a study, did not find these disparate impact in terms of effects of discrimination in the areas in which Colorado exists."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the first indication that the contracting commitment would not be used is this memorandum of August 24, 2001."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Commerce Department implemented that decision, and there's no evidence to the contrary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. But the -- what there is is a Department of Justice requirement imposed upon all Federal agencies not to employ race-conscious remedies in those areas --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And finally, Your Honor, the United States told this Court that the benchmark study is overdue, and I know in my bones, as I know that this case has gone on forever by the United States' effort to make it go on forever and with broad jurisdiction from this Court, that the day this case ends is the day the benchmark study comes out, and suddenly and miraculously Colorado is back in the underutilized category and all these mechanisms apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have a brand new SCC that's been changed and it won't be quite so -- quite so non-narrowly tailored. But there still is an SCC in place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:00 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2001-00-730",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b81f1aab9317c8cc0141146b8a2d124f6ecbdc7c57ce7dc0db3bfd759cacaddd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b81f1aab9317-0003-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the day this Court says it's moot is the day Adarand gets standing again because it loses another contract because this program is applied in Colorado, and Adarand will start this sad process again."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
